  "body": "If you want to build on something else like alpine, it seems you have to copy lots of files from github. Can't these be included in pip packages or so?\r\n\r\nIn the old Dockerfile I think you had the pip install matrix-[xxx] packages are these still being updated?\r\n\r\nI assume this \r\n`COPY synapse /synapse/synapse/`\r\ncopies the whole synapse dir from github not? Why is this? Why is this not a package?\r\n\r\nIf you keep the docker file more like the install manual[1], it also prevents having different bugs being reported from docker images and python packages. I think it is better to distribute the packages and work everywhere with the packages.\r\n\r\n[1]\r\n https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/develop/INSTALL.md",
